\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Continuous-trajectory safety constraints and ALM correction. Top: trajectories and control points for the reference state $\mathbf  Q^{\mathrm  {ref}}$ and its safety-corrected state. Bottom: joint subdivision by region responsibility intervals and B-spline knots. The inset constrains the four control points $\bm  {\beta }_{k,j}$ to $\mathcal  R_{\rho (k)}$, ensuring continuous containment by the convex-hull property. Point and region counts are illustrative, not experimental settings.}}{5}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:alm}{{3}{5}{Continuous-trajectory safety constraints and ALM correction. Top: trajectories and control points for the reference state $\mathbf Q^{\mathrm {ref}}$ and its safety-corrected state. Bottom: joint subdivision by region responsibility intervals and B-spline knots. The inset constrains the four control points $\boldsymbol \beta _{k,j}$ to $\mathcal R_{\rho (k)}$, ensuring continuous containment by the convex-hull property. Point and region counts are illustrative, not experimental settings}{figure.3}{}}
